# Spline Studio

**A visual spline creation and editing tool for OMSI 2 and openOMSI.**

[한국어](README_KO.md) | [Download](https://github.com/OMSI2Merzoa/OMSI-SplineStudio/releases) | [Report an Issue](https://github.com/OMSI2Merzoa/OMSI-SplineStudio/issues)

---

## About

Spline Studio is a dedicated tool designed to simplify the creation and editing of spline (SLI) files for OMSI 2 and openOMSI map development.

Instead of manually editing coordinates, texture mappings, and AI paths in SLI files, map creators can work within a visual editing environment.

From simple roads to complex road cross-sections, Spline Studio provides tools for creating new splines and modifying existing ones.

Spline Studio is available free of charge for both beginners and experienced map creators.

## Features

### Spline Creation and Editing

- Import and export existing SLI files
- Visual 2D cross-section editing
- Precise coordinate editing
- Component-based automatic spline generation
- Traffic lanes, sidewalks, curbs, gutters, and fixed-width bus bays
- Mirroring and linked components
- Road crossfall and transverse slope settings
- Road variants based on existing splines
- Spline comparison and multi-selection editing

### 3D Preview

- Real-time 3D preview
- Straight, curved, and sloped spline previews
- Multiple camera viewpoints
- Driver's perspective preview
- Preview image export

### Textures and Materials

- Visual UV mapping editor
- Texture previews and instant texture application
- Texture mapping presets
- Batch texture replacement
- Platform-specific material settings for OMSI 2 and openOMSI
- PBR resource management for openOMSI

### AI Paths

- Vehicle and pedestrian path creation
- Right-hand and left-hand traffic support
- Automatic AI path generation based on road components
- AI path position and direction editing

### Project and Resource Management

- Multi-spline project management
- Shared project texture resources
- Missing resource detection and relinking
- Batch spline export
- Distribution ZIP package creation
- Project backup and restoration
- Autosave and recovery

### Usability

- Korean and English language support
- Dark, light, and system themes
- Simple and advanced editing modes
- User-defined presets
- Example projects
- Built-in help documentation
- GitHub-based automatic updates
- Portable application

